      "images": [],
      "sourceEvidence": {
        "file": "content/batch-001/sources/aspca-cat-litter-box-problems.html",
        "excerpt": "trying to show your cat that her litter box is safe by placing her in the box will likely backfire"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "knowledge-033",
      "contentType": "knowledge",
      "title": "听见猫叫，先看看它在表达什么",
      "text": "猫叫可能是在打招呼、寻找互动、期待食物，或表示某件事不对劲。先检查饮水、猫砂盆和通行是否正常，再结合当时场景观察，别一律理解为任性讨要。ASPCA提醒，除了明确知道它在索取某种回应的情况，忽视叫声可能错过真实需要。",
      "topics": [
        "养宠经验"
      ],
      "circleId": "circle-cats",
      "editorId": "catalog-cat-behavior",
      "source": {
        "title": "Meowing and Yowling",
        "publisher": "ASPCA",
        "author": "ASPCA",
        "url": "https://www.aspca.org/pet-care/cat-care/common-cat-behavior-issues/meowing-and-yowling",
        "checkedAt": "2026-09-29"
      },
      "review": {
        "status": "approved",
        "reviewer": "有宠有邻内容整理",
        "reviewedAt": "2026-09-29"
      },
      "images": [],
      "sourceEvidence": {
        "file": "content/batch-001/sources/aspca-cat-meowing-and-yowling.html",
        "excerpt": "Always make sure that her needs are met before assuming that she’s just being demanding"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "knowledge-034",
      "contentType": "knowledge",
      "title": "用叫声日记寻找反复出现的线索",
      "text": "想调整频繁叫声，先记录何时发生、周围有什么，以及什么事情会让猫安静下来。可能是饭点、见到人、门窗附近，或某段独处时间。ASPCA建议用记录寻找规律，同时由兽医排除导致不适的健康问题；观察具体情境，比只数叫了多少次更有帮助。",
      "topics": [
        "养宠经验"
      ],
